# DSSTech (Revit)

Revit add-in (hosts 2025–2027) plus a Revit-independent engine:

`Revit object → WorkItem → norm leaf-code → adjustment → VL/NC/M`

It is **not** OneX, Forma, Electron, APS copy, or an IFC viewer. Ignore any inherited OneX/Forma North Star for this workspace.

Open `DSSTech.sln`. Namespaces are `DSSTech.*` and `Dss.*`. The installed assembly is `DSSTech.dll`, class `DSSTech.Revit.App`. Do not recreate `QSNormEngine.sln` or `src/QSNormEngine.*`. Shared parameter names stay `QS_*`. The quantity schedule name stays `QS-BIM Khối lượng cấu kiện`.

## North Star

- One ribbon tab **DSSTech**, panels left to right: **Thiết lập · Setup**, **CAD → BIM**, **Khối lượng · Quantity**, **Trợ lý AI · AI**. Button labels are bilingual; layout lives in `src/DSSTech.Revit/App.cs` and `docs/RIBBON_UI.md`.
- **Chọn định mức / Norm Selector** on selected elements: results grid + CSV/JSON. `TransactionMode.Manual` so user-confirmed fill/write-back can run. It does **not** auto-write on open.
- **Dựng mô hình / Model Revit** builds from a CAD link the user has already moved and rotated. Base/Top come from the open plan and the next level up; the settings window can adjust them before create.
- Control Center is a dockable pane (parameters, QC, Excel, CAD, AI). QC Auto-Fix stays disabled until a rule sheet exists.
- SQLite is the governed master; `Data/norm-engine-runtime.json` is a generated cache (do not hand-edit as source of truth).
- `SelectedQc1` / `SelectedCodeOnly` / `CanIssueOfficially=false` are **not** official issue.
- Concrete selection requires explicit construction method unless config says otherwise.
- `QS_WorkItemId` is an override, not the primary classification path.
- No dedicated app server. CLI (`DSSTech.Cli`) tests `ElementFacts` JSON outside Revit. MCP is the in-Revit host plus `Dss.RevitMcp` stdio sidecar.

